      <h1 style="color: #e74c3c; font-weight: bold;">Refund Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-muted">Last updated: February 2026</p>
      <hr>

      <h3>$BEEP &amp; Your Wallet</h3>
      <p>Your $BEEP tokens always stay in your own Cardano wallet. SportsBeep never takes custody of them — holding $BEEP simply unlocks play credit to wager with inside the game.</p>

      <div class="panel panel-default" style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
        <div class="panel-heading">
          <h4 class="panel-title">$BEEP Play Credit &amp; Your Cardano Wallet</h4>
        </div>
        <div class="panel-body">
          <ul>
            <li>Your real $BEEP tokens always remain in your own Cardano wallet — SportsBeep never takes custody of them</li>
            <li>Holding $BEEP unlocks play credit you can wager with inside SportsBeep</li>
            <li>Loading or removing play credit only adjusts your in-game balance; no tokens are ever moved on-chain</li>
            <li>You must have a valid Cardano wallet address linked to unlock play credit</li>
            <li>Because no on-chain transfer occurs, there are no blockchain network fees when adjusting play credit</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Contest Entry Refunds</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>If a contest is cancelled before it begins, all entry fees will be refunded in full</li>
        <li>If a contest does not reach the minimum number of entries, it will be cancelled and entry fees refunded</li>
        <li>Once a contest has started (games are in progress), entry fees are non-refundable</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Bonus and Promotional Credits</h3>
      <p>In cases where a user has received a bonus or other promotional $BEEP token benefits and has not yet played through them (entering contests whose total entry fees equal the value of the bonus), SportsBeep reserves the right to refuse the withdrawal and/or close the user's account.</p>

      <h3>Anti-Fraud</h3>
      <p>SportsBeep conducts anti-fraud checks on playing patterns and deposits prior to processing withdrawals. We reserve the right to delay or deny withdrawals if suspicious activity is detected.</p>

